CHEYENNE
FRONTIER DAYS
World's Largest Outdoor Rodco&Western Celebration
PO. Box 2477 Cheyenne, WY 82003 ·(307) 778-7220 • www.cfdrodeo.com
January 23,2024
Mayor Patrick Collins
City Council Members
City of Cheyenne
2101O'Neil Avenue
CheyenneWY82001
Dear Mayor Collins and City Council Members:
My apologies, this letter is to replace the previous letter dated January16,2024, as there is a correction
to the sponsorship level for Bison Beverage.
As you know Cheyenne Frontier Days relies heavily on sponsors/partners to help produce the“Daddyof
‘em All."One of which is Bison Beverage who has sponsored our show overthirty years.
Priorto2009, nonprofit corporations who pulled malt beverage permits for their annual events were
prohibited from receiving sponsorship in the form ofmoney, product or other items of value.In2009,
to a malt beverage licensee to support annual community events if certain requirements were met.That
portionof the statute now reads:
"With prior approval of the applicable licensing authority, malt beverage industry
representatives may furnish, give or lend money or other things of value to a licensee to support
annual community events open to the public if thelicensee:
(i)
Is a nonprofit corporation organized under the laws of thisstate:
(i)
Is qualified as a taxexempt organization under the Internal Revenue Code: and
(ii)
Has been in continuous operation fora period of notless than two (2) years."
Therefore, pursuant to the above statute, Cheyenne Frontier Days is requesting the approval of the
Cheyenne City Council fora two(2)year Bronze Arrowhead Sponsor relationship between Cheyenne
Frontier Days and Bison Beverage for2024&2025.Therequest for approval is specific only to the
annual community event known as Cheyenne Frontier Days, whichisopen to the public, and would
apply to the following specific time frames, involving application to the Cheyenne City Clerk for malt
beverages:
July 19 -28, 2024
July 18-27,2025
For your reference the following documents are included:
```

